      "context_id": "CTX_REVIEW_043",
      "version": 1,
      "statement": "Mathematical scopes of the family-043 old-draft review: general finite-etale transfer and its full fixed-determinant Betti application, exact Koszul/Kummer algebra, known comparison baselines, and the separately unresolved full-P=W target. No historical objective or verdict is a current instruction or acceptance.",
      "definitions": {
        "moduli": "Smooth coprime fixed-determinant spaces for a smooth projective complex curve, g>=2, composite n>=4, gcd(n,d)=1, except prime-rank background claims.",
        "Gamma": "Pic^0(C)[n]; full cohomology includes every nontrivial character summand.",
        "R": "(n^2-1)(g-1).",
        "b": "n(n-1)/2 in the moduli application; general auxiliary bundle rank in the transfer theorem.",
        "weights": "W is the actual Deligne weight filtration; half weight is half its index.",
        "P": "The normalized perverse filtration for the proper Hitchin map, compared with half weights under nonabelian Hodge.",
        "transfer": "f:T->S smooth separated finite type over a smooth complex base, relative complex dimension delta; finite closed torus-affine relative refinements and one common-class, common-actual-center delta+2b filtration at a specified parameter.",
        "historical_sources": "Read-only 9000043/research/MATH_STATE.json and determinant_cover_transfer/report.md; exact historical versions, citations, roles and evidence are mapped in research/DRAFT_REVIEW_INDEX.json.",
        "assumption_provenance": "External assumptions below reuse the historical proposition statements, canonical source versions, locators, and original filed_by=engineer:copilot. Historical Reviewer opinions are not copied as current evidence."
      },
      "content_hash": "7404db70fbd80c808ee5d550239a4f0f5271a645e14baf87f1b43737ea5c0d71"
    }
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "C_FINITE_ETALE_TRANSFER",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_REVIEW_043",
        "content_hash": "7404db70fbd80c808ee5d550239a4f0f5271a645e14baf87f1b43737ea5c0d71"
      },
      "natural_statement": "Under the transfer hypotheses, every finite etale cover has Hodge--Tate rational fiber cohomology, integral ordinary and compact-support local constancy, natural ordinary fiber base change, and ordinary curious Lefschetz with actual-weight center delta at the specified parameter. All lifted components are retained; on a Galois-covered piece the rational cohomology is the full component permutation module tensored with base cohomology. No integral pullback isomorphism is asserted.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [
        {
          "assumption_id": "DELIGNE_STRICTNESS",
          "statement": "The category of rational mixed Hodge structures is abelian, with induced/quotient filtrations on kernels/cokernels; every morphism is strict for weights, so weight gradeds of exact sequences are exact.",
          "source": "Deligne, Theorie de Hodge II, primary PDF retained and statement read.",
          "source_id": "doi:10.1007/BF02684692",
          "locator": "Theorem 2.3.5(i)-(iii) and rational variant 2.3.8",
          "filed_by": "engineer:copilot",
          "content_hash": "49bb4e0fb7a5138714b7a5d0127e86723c150168370605c13783e3f2b1329787"
        },
        {
          "assumption_id": "SAITO_FUNCTORIAL_MHS",
          "statement": "The algebraic derived direct/inverse image, duality and tensor/internal-Hom functors lift to mixed Hodge modules compatibly with rational constructible realization.",
          "source": "Saito, Mixed Hodge Modules, primary published PDF retained and statement read.",
          "source_id": "doi:10.2977/prims/1195171082",
          "locator": "Theorem 0.1, p. 222",
          "filed_by": "engineer:copilot",
          "content_hash": "f668fe1c71953e76cf38f0c01aa2f7c9cb6ca3d78230ac7d73ef15b927f275df"
        },
        {
          "assumption_id": "VERDIER_RELATIVE",
          "statement": "For sheaves over a commutative coefficient ring and f_! of finite cohomological dimension, the canonical map Rf_* RHom(F,f^!G) -> RHom(Rf_!F,G) is an isomorphism. The local-submersion tensor/product formulas identify f^!Z with the relative orientation complex; for a smooth complex map of relative dimension delta this is Z[2delta].",
          "source": "Verdier, Dualite dans la cohomologie des espaces localement compacts, Bourbaki expose 300; actual primary formulas read in the retained PDF images.",
          "source_id": "numdam:SB_1964-1966__9__337_0",
          "locator": "Section 1 coefficient convention; Section 3 equation (3.3) and theorem, pp. 343-344; Section 5 equations (5.1)-(5.2), p. 348",
          "filed_by": "engineer:copilot",
          "content_hash": "2b9492dd6b0415256b27864c3f318ba337cfb6ab20b022acca1c57e74682dd88"
        }
      ],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "0350af8f33ec3e5b8116729530ad866d2a5f409a24e4c64a043fd81c4d593677"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C_BETTI_CHL",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_REVIEW_043",
        "content_hash": "7404db70fbd80c808ee5d550239a4f0f5271a645e14baf87f1b43737ea5c0d71"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For the stated composite coprime fixed-determinant spaces, full H*(X^B,Q) is Hodge--Tate, e has nonzero image in Gr^W_4 H^2, and e^i:Gr^W_(2R-2i) H^m -> Gr^W_(2R+2i) H^(m+2i) is an isomorphism for all i>=0 and m. This includes every Gamma-character summand.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [
        {
          "assumption_id": "MELLIT_STRATIFICATIONS",
          "statement": "The actual ordered flagged GL_n family has rank-b auxiliary torus-affine stratifications: at regular semisimple parameters the common compact-support actual-weight center is delta+2b; over the whole generic ordered V including collisions the relative affine-bundle refinements are vector bundles over A^a x (C*)^s x V by projection.",
          "source": "Mellit, Toric stratifications of character varieties, published 2025; primary-source research task read the exact published locators and their preprint counterparts.",
          "source_id": "doi:10.1007/s10240-025-00158-0",
          "locator": "Definition 4.9; Theorem 6.14; Sections 7.2 and 7.4; Theorem 7.5; proof of Proposition 8.7",
          "filed_by": "engineer:copilot",
          "content_hash": "fa20ae3c89ee0aa72f80f85f6f5310e0c4d7471c1a123f3c1faf1a7cf75254f4"
        },
        {
          "assumption_id": "SAITO_DIRECT_IMAGE",
          "statement": "The algebraic derived direct-image and fiber-restriction functors on mixed Hodge modules realize the usual rational constructible functors, with their natural comparison morphisms.",
          "source": "Saito, Mixed Hodge Modules, primary published PDF retained and statement read.",
          "source_id": "doi:10.2977/prims/1195171082",
          "locator": "Theorem 0.1, p. 222",
          "filed_by": "engineer:copilot",
          "content_hash": "0b57a62c1f24eace949c8c96c4e77a00d4c3beb58a75d431b295450816e4aa33"
        },
        {
          "assumption_id": "SAITO_SMOOTH_VARIATIONS",
          "statement": "Over a smooth complex base and field coefficients, smooth mixed Hodge modules, whose underlying perverse sheaf is a shifted local system, correspond after the dimension shift to admissible graded-polarizable variations of mixed Hodge structure.",
          "source": "Saito, Extension of mixed Hodge modules, primary published PDF retained and Section 3.2 read.",
          "source_id": "numdam:CM_1990__74_2_209_0",
          "locator": "Section 3.2, equation (3.2.1), p. 226",
          "filed_by": "engineer:copilot",
          "content_hash": "47350e33c110645909777c30dd8f16d5f2b2fa4c0341756450f5cc81d222fb63"
        },
        {
          "assumption_id": "DCMS_VARIANT_BOUND",
          "statement": "For p the smallest prime divisor of n and c=n(n-n/p)(g-1), P_{k-c} H_var^k = H_var^k in arbitrary rank.",
          "source": "de Cataldo, Maulik and Shen, arXiv:2002.03336v1; read in the primary HTML.",
          "source_id": "arxiv:2002.03336v1",
          "locator": "Proposition 1.4",
          "filed_by": "engineer:copilot",
          "content_hash": "9f57083e788768f5eaa5ab5fa47331b263784aed3280c89a8ae7bb280f4118b3"
        },
        {
          "assumption_id": "MS_PROJECTIVE_GENERATION",
          "statement": "The projective tautological classes with Chern-character indices j>=2 generate rational cohomology of the PGL_n Dolbeault moduli space, equivalently the Gamma-invariant summand of the coprime fixed-determinant space.",
          "source": "Maulik--Shen, final primary preprint; projective-bundle setup read with the statement.",
          "source_id": "arxiv:2209.02568v2",
          "locator": "Section 2.1, Theorem 2.1(i)",
          "filed_by": "engineer:copilot",
          "content_hash": "e43d3557f9f420003628f77b05fc2163ff1b0130e0ecee37e7a1d278939c7e3d"
        }
      ],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
